<FONT SIZE="2" FACE="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">
I got tired of my system locking almost everytime I zoned.  So, I figured it must be my no longer supported Voodoo 4 Vid card. <P>So..using the hammer theory,  I coughed up the money for a GeForce 3 video card and another 128MEG of RAM.  The RAM, OMG is that stuff cheap!  $30 for 128 MEG!  Buy the stuff now, no reason not to upgrade yer system to 256+.<P>So..I get home and slap the card and the memory in.  Go thru the install process, download the newest Detonator 3 driver from NVidia and fire up one of the demos that came with the card...crash!  Reboot, then try EQ...login, see the zone, crash!  Reboot...many more times.<P>Okay...goto the Vid card Website and read the FAQ.  Turns out that there might be some BIOS updates that I need to do, so I track down my Motherboard website ( <A HREF="http://www.asus.com" TARGET=_blank>www.asus.com</A>  )and find out that there is an new BIOS for my motherboard. It even had some AGP patches. They even a handy program that checks your BIOS version with their website and tells you if there is a patch, then installs it for you.  It did take a few tries to get the BIOS to get applied though.  So just keep hitting the "Retry" button.  After it was done applying the BIOS update, the program said to reboot and hit the DELETE key during boot to enter the BIOS setup program to check the settings.  I noticed my RAM speed was set to 100 instead of 133, so I adjusted that and I think that was all I noticed that was not what I thought it should be.<P>Not one lockup while zoning yesterday afternoon and zero video lag during battle.  With Verser singing during battle and spells going off, I usually had to goto 3rd person to keep the framerate up enough for twisting, but not with the new card!  It rocks!<P>So..lacking a new video card...check your BIOS to make sure it's up to date.  Buy more RAM too.<P>--------------------<P>Verser - Bard of the 51st Song
